================================================================================
HOW TO READ THIS FILE
================================================================================

This is the Apache-2.0 Section 4(d) attribution aggregation point for Anvil.

Two rules govern every entry below, and both come from the licence audit in
research/13-license-compatibility-audit.md as corrected by
research/13a-license-audit-adversarial-review.md:

  1. Every licence recorded here was determined by READING THE LICENSE FILE
     BODY, never by trusting package-manager or registry metadata. Seven
     audited artifacts return NOASSERTION over a real licence, and one hides a
     restrictive licence behind a permissive tag: fdtn-ai/Foundation-Sec-8B is
     tagged apache-2.0 on Hugging Face while its own NOTICE.md states the
     weights remain under the Llama 3.1 Community License and only Cisco's
     delta is Apache-2.0. That artifact is not used by Anvil, but the trap it
     represents is why this rule exists.

  2. An attribution duty is recorded here when it is OWED, and the condition
     that triggers it is stated. Apache-2.0 Section 4(d) attaches to
     distribution of a Derivative Work. Anvil invokes several tools as separate
     subprocesses rather than linking them, so their notice duties trigger at
     IMAGE BUILD and RELEASE PACKAGING, not at source checkout. Those entries
     are marked accordingly rather than being silently omitted or silently
     claimed.

Share-alike sources are deliberately NOT aggregated into this file. They are
quarantined under data/share-alike/, each with its own LICENSE, so that their
copyleft terms cannot propagate into Anvil's own findings database. The pointer
at the end of this file names them; it carries no share-alike content.

